Complexity Analysis
Let m be the number of rows and n be the number of columns.
- Time Complexity: \(O(m \times n)\) — two traversals of the grid.
- Space Complexity: \(O(m+n)\) — two arrays for row and column counts.
Key takeaway: Instead of checking every server against every other server, precompute row and column counts. This makes the solution much more efficient.
